 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZNG8aes05L/",
 "title": "Why Low Cold Call Volume Fails to Get Clients",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains why starting with a tiny volume of 10 cold calls a week is insufficient for acquiring clients. He breaks down the conversion rate math showing that 100 daily dials yield 40 conversations, 4 booked meetings, 2 actual meetings, and eventually sales. High call volume gives salespeople a significantly higher probability of winning compared to competitors.",
 "key_points": [
  "Aim for 10 conversations per day rather than just 10 dials a week.",
  "Out of 100 daily dials with an assumed 40% pick-up rate, you get 40 conversations.",
  "Converting 10% of 40 conversations results in 4 booked meetings.",
  "Out of 4 booked meetings, typically 2 people show up (2 attended meetings).",
  "Completing at least 10 attended meetings results in 1 sale.",
  "Making 10 calls daily for 30 days yields 300 calls total.",
  "Making 100 calls daily for 30 days yields 3,000 calls total, giving competitors a much higher probability of winning."
 ],
 "content": "Post Text: Starting small is an excuse. Make a note of this post. Transcript: \"I'm going to start doing 10 calls every week.\" \"Hey.\" \"Yeah.\" \"10 cold calls?\" \"Yeah. I want to start small.\" \"Why?\" \"Because I don't want to like overdo and then I like...\" \"Let me reframe this for you. Have ten conversations a day, not dials.\" \"Is it a day or a week?\" \"Day, baby! So if you guys want to know the numbers, here is what it is. It's 100 dials. Your pick up rate is... assume 40%. For 100 calls, you'll end up having 40 conversations. Of this, if you put 10%, it is 4 meetings. Of this, two people will show up. That's two meetings! You do at least ten meetings, you make one sale! You can do 10 calls every day for 30 days, and you reach 300 calls. And your competitors are doing 100 calls a day, 30 days, doing 3000 calls! Who has a higher probability of winning?\" Text on screen: This is why you're not getting clients; 100 dials; 40% -> pick up -> 40 convos; -> 10% -> 4 meetings; -> 2 meetings; 10 min -> 1 sale; 10 call d x 30 -> 300; 100 call x 30 -> 3000",
